# SHACL closure: types the PROV-O ontology's own self-description as PROV-O
# data. The published ontology document (fetched as background/closure data
# for this block via bblock.json's "ontology" field) describes itself with:
#
#   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#>
#       a owl:Ontology ;
#       owl:versionIRI <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o-20130430> ;
#       prov:specializationOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o> ;
#       prov:wasRevisionOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o-20130312> .
#
# prov:specializationOf and prov:wasRevisionOf both have domain and range
# prov:Entity, but the ontology never asserts `a prov:Entity` for any of the
# three IRIs it uses as subject/object of those properties (owl:Ontology is
# not declared a subclass of prov:Entity either) -- an untyped-but-implied
# gap in the published RDF, not a data error in any consuming example.
#
# These identifiers are immutable (dated/versioned W3C namespace URIs, not
# subject to further change), so it is safe to assert their PROV typing here
# once rather than special-case the resulting sh:class violations. Reused by
# CDO-Shapes-PROV-O's exemplars.ttl test fixture, which triggers exactly
# this gap; without this closure, ogc.model.cross-domain.prov's own test run
# against that fixture fails 4 constraints that are about the ontology's
# self-description, not about the fixture's actual example data.

@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .

<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o>          a prov:Entity .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#>         a prov:Entity .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o-20130312> a prov:Entity .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o-20130430> a prov:Entity .
